  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender Responsive Peacebuilding in Extractive Industries in Isabel Province, Solomon Islands</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this project is to provide women in communities adjacent to extractive industries in Isabel Province in the Solomon Islands with the enabling environment, skills and networks to more effectively access and lead rights-based dispute resolution processes in both informal and formal decision-making spaces, including in the justice system. The overarching goal is to achieve an environment conducive to peacebuilding, that systematically includes women in local peace building processes through enhanced gender equity and women&apos;s empowerment.</narrative>
  </description>
